@startuml sequence_diagram_password_recovery
title SD 3 - Password recovery
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false

actor "System user" as User
box "SPA" #F3F7FD
  participant PasswordRecoveryPage as Page
  participant authApi as Client
end box
box "Backend" #F5F8F5
  participant "Recovery routes / controller" as API
  participant PasswordRecoveryService as Service
  participant UserRepository as Users
  participant PostgresRecoveryTokenRepository as Tokens
  participant SmtpRecoveryDeliveryAdapter as Delivery
end box
participant "SMTP server" as SMTP

note over API
  Both endpoints apply the public rate limit and validate the request.
  Invalid input or throttling returns 400 or 429.
end note

== Request a link ==
User -> Page : enter account email
Page -> Client : requestPasswordRecovery(email)
Client -> API : POST /api/v1/auth/password-recovery
API -> Service : requestRecovery(email)
Service -> Users : findByEmail(canonical email)
Users --> Service : User or no account
opt Account has a local password
  Service -> Service : generate token, digest and expiry
  group PostgreSQL transaction
    Service -> Tokens : replaceActive(userId, digest, expiresAt, tx)
    Tokens --> Service : invalidate earlier links and store new digest
  end
  opt Token stored
    Service -> Delivery : sendRecoveryLink(account email, link)
    Delivery -> SMTP : submit email
    SMTP --> Delivery : accepted or failed
    Delivery --> Service : outcome
    note right of Service
      The service logs delivery failures.
      The public response stays generic.
    end note
  end
end
Service --> API : request handled
API --> Client : 202 Accepted
Client --> Page : generic confirmation

== Complete recovery ==
User -> Page : open link and submit new password
Page -> Client : completePasswordRecovery(token, password)
Client -> API : POST /api/v1/auth/password-recovery/complete
API -> Service : completeRecovery(token, password)
alt New password fails policy
  Service --> API : 422 password policy error
else Valid password format
  Service -> Service : hash token
  group One PostgreSQL transaction
    Service -> Tokens : findUsableForUpdate(digest, tx)
    Tokens --> Service : eligible account ID or no result
    opt Usable token
      Service -> Users : findById(accountId, tx)
      Users --> Service : User with current credential, if present
    end
    alt Invalid token, missing local password or exact password reuse
      Service -> Service : reject and roll back
    else Valid token and eligible replacement
      Service -> Service : hash new password
      Service -> Tokens : consumeAndUpdatePassword(digest, userId, hash, tx)
      Tokens --> Service : changed or no eligible update
    end
  end
  Service --> API : success or 422 if rejected
end
API --> Client : 204 No Content or error
Client --> Page : show result

note over Service,Tokens
  A usable link is current, unexpired and unused.
  Token consumption and password update commit together.
end note
@enduml
